{"id": "EUVD-2026-103551", "enisaUuid": "8e66904d-9518-3092-b2b9-9bcc7dafc14a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: arm64: Do not clear VM-wide SVE feature on vCPU init failure\n\npkvm_vcpu_init_sve() clears KVM_ARM_VCPU_SVE in kvm->arch.vcpu_features\nwhen it fails, but vcpu_has_sve() tests KVM_ARCH_FLAG_GUEST_HAS_SVE,\nwhich is left set. Later vCPUs on that VM then skip the SVE setup and\nregister with a NULL sve_state, which the guest's first FP access hands\nto sve_load_state().\n\nReturn the error without touching vcpu_features.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:20:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:23:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bd46b41f412fb81c50bac1a0929ec31320f3a807", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f0cd8ffae092cc1b9d7cfa9188ed5a88a374adcb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a1b3c788ad31837e348075e93dbba3f447492776"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98637", "GHSA-j9wj-wgv2-phcm"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2be4de7a-a920-3223-a0ad-14f057bd4251", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3af5b9f2-c71b-343a-bca9-95cd86d03fa0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "519574a3-0ea6-3517-9ade-9a80a08fbca6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5db1bef933427aa467ad89c7b695a84a6b4afe16 <a1b3c788ad31837e348075e93dbba3f447492776"}, {"id": "6cc249d9-761d-3ebd-8d0f-c9bdca9bf71c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "859d6f9b-b4b4-36cf-a750-99e011ff4c98", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.16"}, {"id": "a8e4ed3a-4178-3a91-bc06-7bd31280bd53", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5db1bef933427aa467ad89c7b695a84a6b4afe16 <bd46b41f412fb81c50ba